From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:11:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Sable header, Recents rows, dial pad keys and
 in-call pills

Phone controls in the shape of the Sable Phone design
(sable-phone-dialer-titan2), on the palette of the previous patch:

* Header: "Phone" (the app label, 22sp ScreenTitle) at the start of the
  top bar with the search pill beside it. The title is a heading for
  screen readers and is not focusable. The search pill gets an
  outline-tone border that turns accent while it has focus.
* Recents: the caller row (primary_action_view) takes the Sable row
  background, so the focused call shows the accent outline; cards use
  12dp corners. Day labels ("Today") and the Favorites/Suggestions
  headers use the Sable section label (12sp, caps, accent tone); the
  favourites "Add" button is an outlined pill.
* Dial pad: every key is an outlined pill tile on the dark pad (inset
  inside its cell, so the touch target is the whole cell as before),
  with an accent border on focus; digits are white. The number being
  dialled sits in an accent-outlined field. The key background stays a
  RippleDrawable, as DialpadView requires.
* In-call: Mute, Keypad, Audio, Add, Hold and Video are rounded panels
  (icon and label inside, accent while on, accent border on focus), and
  End is a 112dp danger pill (dark red, light red border), flat.

No Java change. Focus order, touch targets, the M/S/D and Space keys of
the earlier patches and every upstream function are unchanged.
